{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JpYvkoUVthP9ZzpmWu","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Before I draft, a few questions. Your answers will change what the comment says.\n\n1. **What do you want the commission to do instead?** You could ask them to keep 4, go to 3, set a separate charter limit (charters land 9% and private boats land 80%), shorten the cut to fewer than 3 years, or review it after a year. Commissioners are more likely to act on a specific alternative than on a plain \"no.\"\n\n2. **How many trips a season do you need to break even?** I'm asking because of the \"out of business\" line. Your own 2016 numbers show you lost 32 trips and stayed open. If you say \"every boat will close,\" a commissioner will probably point to that. If you can say \"below X trips I can't cover fuel, insurance and the boat payment,\" we can make a strong claim that holds up.\n\n3. **Did any boats in your harbor close or sell after the 2016 cut?** Or are any of the 11 struggling now? A real example would carry a lot of weight.\n\n4. **What did the 2016 cut go from and to?** Was it about the same size as 4 to 2? That tells us whether 2016 is a fair guide to next season.\n\n5. **Did the survey ask how many fewer trips people would book?** Or just whether they'd book fewer? Even rough numbers would help.\n\nIf you don't know some of these, just say so. I'll write around them and won't guess."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":392,"cache_read_input_tokens":9590,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":392},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bb30b52-39a2-4ea2-b845-e432faa4fbb2","uuid":"fb1026b2-f8af-491f-8166-