{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Ch7JqY5vhApbDXentZXQz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I wrote it without \"every boat will go under.\" The 2016 numbers are the problem: you lost 32 trips, nobody in your harbor closed, and you only know your own books. If you say every boat will close, a commissioner can point that out and the rest of your comment loses force. The strongest true version is that 2016 hurt and you never fully recovered, a 3-year cut is worse, and two captains have told you they'd sell. That's specific, it's real, and they can't knock it down.\n\n<final_document>\nGood evening, Commissioners. My name is [NAME]. I've run a charter boat out of [HARBOR] for 22 years. I'm one of 11 charter boats there.\n\nI'm not here to tell you the stock is fine. Your staff says flounder are at 78% of target, and I want them around for the next 22 years too. I'm asking you to get there without cutting the limit to two.\n\nI've been through this before. When the limit was cut in 2016, my bookings fell from 170 trips to 138 the next season. At today's price, that's nearly $29,000 gone in one year. Two years later I'd only climbed back to 155. I never got all the way back.\n\nThat was one cut. This one runs three years. Our charter association asked 70 past customers what they'd do at two fish. Forty-one said they'd book fewer trips. Only 12 said they'd book the same.\n\nTwo captains in my harbor have already told me that if bookings drop like they did in 2016, they'll sell. Three lean years in a row is more than a lot of us can carry.\n\nCharter boats land about 9% of this state's summer flounder. Private boats land about 80%. For a private angler, two fish means a smaller day. For us, it decides whether the customer books at all.\n\nSo I'm asking for either of two things: a three-fish limit, or a shorter season. Either one protects the stock without putting charter boats through three years like the one I had after 2016.\n\nThank you.\n</final_document>\n\nSome notes:\n\n- **Length:** It's about 260 words, which takes roughly two minutes at a steady pace. Read it out loud with a timer once. If you run long, cut the 9%/80% paragraph first.\n- **The dollar figure:** \"Nearly $29,000\" is 32 trips at your current $900 rate. That's why it says \"at today's price.\" If your 2016 rate was different, you can use the real 2016 figure or keep the line as written.\n- **The survey:** Be ready if someone asks about it. It came from your association, and it only asked whether people would book fewer trips, not how many fewer. Saying that openly will make you more credible.\n- **Before the meeting:** Try to work out roughly how many trips a season you need to cover your costs. If a commissioner asks \"would you actually go under?\", that number is the best answer you could give."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":895,"cache_read_input_tokens":9982,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":895},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7bb30b52-39a2-4ea2-b845-e432faa4fbb2","uuid":"f0f341d7-f572-4dad-b42a-594d67d18616","timestamp":"2026-11-16T21:22:12.853Z","request_id":"req_011Ch7JqXxV5cQNk9JUAAFEq"}
